In programming, a Model class is generally a data-holder class. It represents the data of some entity.

User is the Model because it represents what a User looks like.
Model
  ↓
"What data does a User have?"

User
 ├── id
 ├── name
 ├── email
 ├── age
 └── role

It generally doesn't contain business logic.

User              → Model / data
UserRepository    → stores & retrieves Users
UserService       → business logic
UserController    → API/request handling
